# Line-ending policy.
#
# This project is developed on Windows and gated on Windows CI, and it is
# checked by tools that are whitespace-sensitive: `cargo fmt --check` and
# `oxlint`. Without an explicit policy, whether a file is stored with LF or
# CRLF depends on each contributor's `core.autocrlf`, so the same source can
# produce a format-check failure on one machine and a clean pass on another,
# and a reformatting churn diff that hides the real change under review.
#
# So: every text file is stored as LF in the repository, and Git converts to
# the platform-native form on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Text: stored LF ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.rs                          text eol=lf
*.toml                        text eol=lf
*.py                          text eol=lf
*.ts                          text eol=lf
*.tsx                         text eol=lf
*.js                          text eol=lf
*.json                        text eol=lf
*.css                         text eol=lf
*.html                        text eol=lf
*.md                          text eol=lf
*.yml                         text eol=lf
*.yaml                        text eol=lf
*.svg                         text eol=lf

# ── Scripts that Windows requires to be CRLF ───────────────────────
# cmd.exe parses a batch file line by line and mishandles a trailing LF on
# goto/label lines, so these must keep CRLF regardless of the policy above.
*.bat                         text eol=crlf
*.cmd                         text eol=crlf

# ── Binary: never converted, never diffed ──────────────────────────
*.png                         binary
*.jpg                         binary
*.ico                         binary
*.icns                        binary
*.wav                         binary
*.zip                         binary

# ── Lockfiles ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are committed deliberately: they are the only thing that makes a
# dependency install reproducible. They are collapsed in diffs because a
# full resolution tree is noise, not review material.
package-lock.json             -diff linguist-generated
src-tauri/Cargo.lock          -diff linguist-generated
